#import "/prelude.typ": *

#Recipe(
  title: "Sticky Rice",
  yield: [2 servings],
)[
  - Short-grain white rice #WN #aside[250mL]
  - 250mL water
  - Salt, to taste #WN #VN

  Equipment:
  - Rice cooker#Fn.rice-cooker
][
  + RINSE rice in cold water 4-5 times, or until water runs clear.
  + PLACE rice in pot.
  + FILL pot fully with cold water.
  + SOAK. #pause[30 min.]
  + STRAIN.
  + RESTORE rice to pot.
  + ADD water & salt.
  + COOK in rice cooker. #pause[\~30 min.]

  == Trivia

  It frankly baffles me that this recipe works. It seems like rinsing the rice not just
  once but effectively twice should get all the loose starches out, which I _believe_ is
  the element that makes sticky rice sticky.#fn[Hang on, is this true?] It ultimately does
  work though, which I guess is pretty cool.

  Oh, also, please do make more rice than prescribed. The more rice, the lower the chance
  of burning, it seems.
]
